{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"KeyboardKit"}],"title":"Dictation","role":"article","images":[{"identifier":"Feature-Dictation.jpg","type":"card"}],"roleHeading":"Article","color":{"standardColorIdentifier":"purple"}},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"This developer guide describes how to set up dictation.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit can perform dictation directly from the keyboard extension by opening the main app to start dictation, then returning to the keyboard to perform dictation. See the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Dictation-Article","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" article for more information about this feature.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"👑 Dictation requires a KeyboardKit Pro license with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/ProFeature\/dictation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" support, unless you want to implement the feature from scratch. You can sign up for KeyboardKit Pro from the "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/keyboardkit.com","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A KeyboardKit keyboard can start dictation with the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAction\/dictation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" action, which calls the controller’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardController\/performDictation()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" function, which in turn uses the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardServices\/dictationService","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to start dictation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/StandardDictationService","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" will open the app to start dictation, then return to the keyboard if it has a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". The dictation then stays alive in the background, and can be started again without opening the app. You can customize this flow, if needed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"How to set up dictation","anchor":"How-to-set-up-dictation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Setting up dictation involves adding all required permissions and capabilities to the app, enabling ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Data-Syncing","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" between the app and its keyboard, and wire up a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationEngine","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" in the main app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Step 1. Add Required Permissions","anchor":"Step-1-Add-Required-Permissions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Before you can start dictation, you must add these required keys to your app’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Info.plist"},{"text":", otherwise your app will crash at runtime:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription<\/key>","<string>Describe why you need microphone access.<\/string>","<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription<\/key>","<string>Describe why you need speech recognition.<\/string>"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is only needed if you use the standard dictation plugin engine. A custom engine may need different permissions, for instance if it sends audio recordings to a custom dictation model.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Step 2. Enable Background Audio","anchor":"Step-2-Enable-Background-Audio","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Since in-keyboard dictation requires that the app is kept alive in the background, you must also enable the background audio capability:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"developer-dictation-background-modes","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["<key>UIBackgroundModes<\/key>","<array>","    <string>audio<\/string>","<\/array>"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you don’t use background audio for anything else, you should explain why you need it in AppStore Connect. Here’s a template."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important","type":"aside"},{"code":["Regarding Audio Background Mode","    ","The keyboard extension in this app has a dictation feature that","launches the main app to start dictation, then reads continuous","updates from the app while the app is in the background.","","Since the app must run in the background, it requires the Audio","Background Mode to avoid that dictation is cancelled. This mode","is only used to keep the dictation alive, and the user can stop","dictation from the main app and keyboard at any time. ","","If you need to locate this feature:","","    1. Enable the keyboard and Full Access in Settings.","    2. Activate the keyboard from any text field.","    3. Start dictation with the keyboard dictation button.","    4. Return to the keyboard to start dictating.","    5. Make sure that the app is not in the foreground.","    6. Verify that dictation is still running.","    7. Verify that you can stop dictation with the mic button.","","Just let us know if you need any more information regarding this."],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Step 3. Set up an App Group","anchor":"Step-3-Set-up-an-App-Group","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To share data between the main app and its keyboard, you must set up an App Group and enable it for both targets. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Data-Syncing","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for more information.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Step 4. Set up a Deep Link","anchor":"Step-4-Set-up-a-Deep-Link","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To make it possible for the keyboard to open the app and start dictation, you must set up a deep link URL scheme to open the main app:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"developer-dictation-url-scheme","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a unique URL scheme for your app to “URL Schemes”, without the “:\/\/” suffix, then add the full scheme to your ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". As you can see in the app above, the official KeyboardKit app uses “keyboardkit:\/\/” as scheme.:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["KeyboardApp(..., deepLinks: .init(app: \"keyboardkit:\/\/\"))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit uses <SCHEME>dictation as default dictation deep link (e.g. “keyboardkit:\/\/dictation”), but you can customize it if needed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Step 5. Set up the Keyboard Extension","anchor":"Step-5-Set-up-the-Keyboard-Extension","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Since dictation will be performed in the main app, your keyboard extension doesn’t have to be configured further. Just follow the steps above, and the keyboard extension will be good to go.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" will automatically show a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationKeyboardOverlay","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" view whenever dictation is active. You can set up a custom view with the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardReplacementOverlay(isPresented:content:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" view modifier.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Step 6. Set up the Main Application","anchor":"Step-6-Set-up-the-Main-Application","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To make the app perform dictation, we can pass a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationEngine","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" that wraps the main app content:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["KeyboardAppView(","    for: .myApp, ","    dictationEngine: ...",") {","    ContentView()","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This will apply a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardDictation(withEngine:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" modifier to the content view, which is much more reliable than applying the modifier yourself. If you use the dictation plugin, this is how easy it is to inject the plugin engine:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import KeyboardKitDictationPlugin  \/\/ <- 1","","extension PluginDictationEngine: @retroactive DictationEngine {}  \/\/ <- 2","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            KeyboardAppView(","                for: .myApp,","                dictationEngine: pluginDictationEngine  \/\/ <- 3","            ) {","                ContentView()","            }","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Plugins-Article","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" article on how to use the standard ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyboardKitDictationPlugin"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you don’t use a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", or need a custom ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationService","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", you can instead apply the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardDictation(withEngine:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardDictation(withService:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" view modifier to a view that’s always visible. Make sure to pass in an engine that’s created once, and not a new engine every time the view is redrawn.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit doesn’t include a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationEngine"},{"type":"text","text":", since that would require "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" apps that use KeyboardKit to add the permissions above, even if they don’t use dictation. By moving the engine to the dictation plugin, an app can choose if it wants to use dictation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Note"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also implement the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationEngine","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" protocol yourself, for instance if you want to integrate with a custom engine or model."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Step 7. Start dictation","level":3,"anchor":"Step-7-Start-dictation"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can now start dictation in your keyboard by triggering the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAction\/dictation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" action, or by calling the controller "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardInputViewController\/performDictation()"},{"type":"text","text":" or service "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationService\/startDictationFromKeyboard()"},{"text":" functions, based on where you start it from. You should prefer using the action.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/StandardDictationService","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" will open the main app with the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp"},{"type":"text","text":" dictation URL, using "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppOpenReason\/dictation"},{"type":"text","text":" as the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext\/openReason"},{"type":"text","text":", and the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppView"},{"type":"text","text":" will start dictation if the open URL matches the deep link."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If dictation was started from a known "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication"},{"type":"text","text":", the main app will try to return to the keyboard to start dictation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","style":"tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Since ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" support is limited, we recommend showing a message in the app to tell the user to tap the top-leading back arrow to return to the keyboard. You can use the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppOpenReasonMessageView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or a custom view.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Tip"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/developer-dictation"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Custom-Keyboards","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Data-Syncing","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Debugging","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-dSYMs","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Experiments","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit